  "configuration_id": "config_016",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only with pca_n2000 (config_001) achieves 48.5% acc, while both image-only models perform poorly (~21-23%), suggesting image features alone are weak. However, it remains unclear whether image features provide complementary information in a multimodal context. Question tested: Does concatenating image features (resnet50) to the RNA representation improve over RNA-only? config_016 is the minimal multimodal extension of config_001 (same RNA encoder, same singleprofile setting, only adding resnet50 image via concat), giving a clean A/B comparison. Why this is the best next experiment: With only 3 data points, the most fundamental design decision is whether the multimodal paradigm adds value at all. Resolving this early prevents wasting budget on 36 multimodal configurations if image features are uninformative, or confirms a promising direction to exploit. The simple concat fusion also avoids confounding from more complex fusion strategies."
